@bio:

Jacek Iwaszko is a musicologist and a graduate of the
Institute of Musicology at the University of Warsaw, where
he received his PhD in 2024. He works in the Research
Department of the Fryderyk Chopin Institute,
where he coordinates digital transcription and software
development in the Institute’s digital projects. His
research interests include music editing and source
studies, as well as digital musicology, with a particular
focus on the encoding and computer-assisted analysis of
Renaissance music.



@@END: BIO